      <bpmn:documentation>obra/superpowers:skills/writing-plans/SKILL.md.

Below this box: a scope check, a file-structure pass, task decomposition into bite-sized steps of two to five minutes each, and a self-review against the spec for coverage, placeholders and type consistency. The plan carries a Global Constraints block copied verbatim from the spec.

The skill ends by offering the human a choice of executor — subagent-driven or inline. This diagram takes the subagent branch only, because students on this course will always have subagents, and draws no gateway for a fork it does not model.</bpmn:documentation>
