      <bpmn:task id="W_tasks" name="Cut right-sized tasks of 2-5 minute steps&#10;writing-plans">
        <bpmn:documentation>obra/superpowers:skills/writing-plans/SKILL.md, "Task Right-Sizing" and "Bite-Sized Task Granularity". A task is the smallest unit that carries its own test cycle and is worth a fresh reviewer's gate; split only where a reviewer could reject one task while approving its neighbor. Each step is one action of 2 to 5 minutes: write the failing test, run it, implement, run again, commit.</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>wf6</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>wf7</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:task>
      <bpmn:task id="W_write" name="Write the plan: header, Global Constraints, every task in full&#10;writing-plans">
        <bpmn:documentation>obra/superpowers:skills/writing-plans/SKILL.md, "Plan Document Header", "Task Structure" and "No Placeholders". Saved to docs/superpowers/plans/YYYY-MM-DD-&lt;feature-name&gt;.md (a user preference overrides the directory). The header names the spec; Global Constraints are copied verbatim from it. Every task lists exact files, Consumes/Produces interfaces, and complete code for every code step: no TBD, no "similar to Task N".

The skill never says to commit the plan, so no git step is drawn here. finishing-a-development-branch later names "uncommitted plans" among the files that can block worktree removal.</bpmn:documentation>
